2. **Session cache bonus scales with input size**: Large session requests (>300 tokens) benefit most from cache hits, so we give extra weight to cache hit rate for those cases.

3. **More gradual KV utilization penalty**: Starting at 0.7 instead of 0.6 gives instances more breathing room before penalizing them. Added a gentle slope from 0.5-0.7 to make the transition smoother.

4. **Differentiated load penalty**: The key insight is that QueueDepth (waiting requests) is more problematic than BatchSize/PendingRequests (active processing). By weighting queue depth 1.4x higher, we better prioritize routing away from truly congested instances while being more tolerant of instances that are busy but not backed up.

